  "courseSlug": "remix-course",
  "courseTitle": "Remix.js - The Practical Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "34675970",
      "title": "Adding Default Error Handling Logic",
      "lectureOrder": 80,
      "videoOrder": 74,
      "sourceHash": "318cf178161782de14af963b1c7e5f6a5e9eaf3cfeb23c876ec9d08a867afc36",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.4,
          "end": 4.41,
          "en": "Now here for the error boundary,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.41,
          "end": 7.95,
          "en": "I essentially wanna return pretty much the same content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.95,
          "end": 10.29,
          "en": "as I do for the catch boundary.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.29,
          "end": 13.623,
          "en": "So here for simplicity reasons, I'll just copy and paste it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.61,
          "end": 17.73,
          "en": "But here, we don't get any error response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.73,
          "end": 21.09,
          "en": "Instead, this component here is rendered by Remix",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.09,
          "end": 23.97,
          "en": "whenever we have any unhandled error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.97,
          "end": 27,
          "en": "generated anywhere in the application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27,
          "end": 32,
          "en": "For example, if we try to get or delete an expense,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 32.67,
          "end": 34.44,
          "en": "and if this would throw an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.44,
          "end": 37.38,
          "en": "and we then just rethrow it, as we're doing it here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.38,
          "end": 39.87,
          "en": "then this would not be an error response,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.87,
          "end": 41.85,
          "en": "but a regular error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.85,
          "end": 44.88,
          "en": "And that would lead to this error boundary component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 44.88,
          "end": 45.723,
          "en": "to be rendered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.95,
          "end": 49.2,
          "en": "Therefore, we got no response where",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 49.2,
          "end": 52.44,
          "en": "we could extract a status text or anything like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 52.44,
          "end": 55.59,
          "en": "But Remix will give us the error object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 55.59,
          "end": 56.55,
          "en": "as a argument.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 56.55,
          "end": 60.45,
          "en": "To be precise, Remix simply sets the error prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 60.45,
          "end": 62.55,
          "en": "on this error boundary component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 62.55,
          "end": 66.39,
          "en": "and we can use this error prop to show a message.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 66.39,
          "end": 69.03,
          "en": "For example, here we can access error.message",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 69.03,
          "end": 71.82,
          "en": "and if that should be undefined, we show something else.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 71.82,
          "end": 74.037,
          "en": "But otherwise, we show the message that is attached",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 74.037,
          "end": 76.293,
          "en": "to the error that was generated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 77.73,
          "end": 80.31,
          "en": "So, that's one way of handling this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 80.31,
          "end": 82.65,
          "en": "Of course, we also might want a title here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 82.65,
          "end": 86.06700000000001,
          "en": "and here we could simply say \"An error occurred.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 86.97,
          "end": 89.34,
          "en": "Now you can definitely set up more sophisticated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 89.34,
          "end": 90.51,
          "en": "error handling,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 90.51,
          "end": 94.38300000000001,
          "en": "but this is a good standard way of handling such errors.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 95.67,
          "end": 99.21000000000001,
          "en": "Now, to also simulate such an error here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 99.21000000000001,
          "end": 103.92,
          "en": "I simply wanna edit my expenses.server code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 103.92,
          "end": 106.89,
          "en": "and edit this deleteExpense function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 106.89,
          "end": 111.84,
          "en": "such that I try to delete an expense where the ID is abc.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 111.84,
          "end": 113.88,
          "en": "So where I hard code this ID,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 113.88,
          "end": 117.06,
          "en": "and this is an invalid ID which does not exist,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 117.06,
          "end": 119.31,
          "en": "and which also does not have the right format",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 119.31,
          "end": 121.05,
          "en": "expected by MongoDB.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 121.05,
          "end": 122.76,
          "en": "So this should cause an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 122.76,
          "end": 125.313,
          "en": "if we try to delete an expense with that ID.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 126.42,
          "end": 130.26,
          "en": "So therefore, now if I go back to my expenses and",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 130.26,
          "end": 132.81,
          "en": "I quickly add a new expense here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 132.81,
          "end": 135.39,
          "en": "so that we have one which I can delete,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 135.39,
          "end": 139.203,
          "en": "and I then try to delete it, I get this error page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 140.34,
          "end": 142.77,
          "en": "But as you can tell, the message I'm getting here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 142.77,
          "end": 146.91,
          "en": "is not necessarily a message I wanna show to my end users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 146.91,
          "end": 150.3,
          "en": "This is the message that was generated by Prisma.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 150.3,
          "end": 151.5,
          "en": "This is hard to read",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 151.5,
          "end": 154.47,
          "en": "and it also might contain some information and data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 154.47,
          "end": 156.663,
          "en": "which I don't wanna expose to my users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 157.92000000000002,
          "end": 160.74,
          "en": "And therefore, here for this error handling,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 160.74,
          "end": 162.84,
          "en": "I actually wanna enhance it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 162.84,
          "end": 166.71,
          "en": "such that I don't rethrow the error that's generated here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 166.71,
          "end": 169.35,
          "en": "but instead I generate a new error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 169.35,
          "end": 172.05,
          "en": "and I throw a new error here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 172.05,
          "end": 175.639,
          "en": "where I have a message that's crafted by me.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 175.639,
          "end": 179.28,
          "en": "Like: \"Failed to delete expense.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 179.28,
          "end": 181.2,
          "en": "And you could be more specific here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 181.2,
          "end": 184.98,
          "en": "but you don't wanna share any details that are very specific",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 184.98,
          "end": 187.77,
          "en": "to your code or your backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 187.77,
          "end": 189.93,
          "en": "A more generic error message is better",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 189.93,
          "end": 192.273,
          "en": "if you wanna show it to your end users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 193.41,
          "end": 195.72,
          "en": "So here I'm using this error message.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 195.72,
          "end": 200.72,
          "en": "Here for updating, I'll say \"Failed to update expense.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 201.27,
          "end": 204.06,
          "en": "And then here for getting expense,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 204.06,
          "end": 208.02,
          "en": "I'll say \"Failed to get expense.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 208.02,
          "end": 209.34,
          "en": "And for getting all expenses,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 209.34,
          "end": 212.37,
          "en": "I'll say \"Failed to get expenses.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 212.37,
          "end": 216,
          "en": "Not very creative, but it should do the job here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 216,
          "end": 220.287,
          "en": "For adding, I'll simply say \"Failed to add expense.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 221.91,
          "end": 225.57,
          "en": "And with that all done, if I save this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 225.57,
          "end": 227.64,
          "en": "and I again try to delete,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 227.64,
          "end": 231.21,
          "en": "and keep in mind that the delete code is still broken,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 231.21,
          "end": 233.31,
          "en": "but if I now try to delete this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 233.31,
          "end": 236.19,
          "en": "you see that now I get this generic error message",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 236.19,
          "end": 237.87,
          "en": "which I set here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 237.87,
          "end": 239.91,
          "en": "And that's also something to keep in mind.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 239.91,
          "end": 241.44,
          "en": "It's not specific to Remix,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 241.44,
          "end": 244.29,
          "en": "but in general when building a web application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 244.29,
          "end": 246.93,
          "en": "you wanna make sure that you don't accidentally share",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 246.93,
          "end": 251.37,
          "en": "error details with your users that shouldn't be shared.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 251.37,
          "end": 253.56,
          "en": "Now, with that, I'll fix this error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 253.56,
          "end": 256.08,
          "en": "and use the proper code again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 256.08,
          "end": 258.54,
          "en": "so that deleting does work again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 258.54,
          "end": 259.41,
          "en": "But this is of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 259.41,
          "end": 261.81,
          "en": "an important topic of which you should be aware.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
